Opus parser
===========

This directory contains a stripped libopus decoder from commit
3da9f7a6db1c05c3996cb363a9d1931a978bf1be (2026-06-12).
Upstream is https://github.com/xiph/opus. The code uses the 3-clause BSD
license in COPYING.

Balrogg needs the entropy-decoder operations in their original order, but
does not need decoded audio. Signal processing, concealment, resampling and
floating-point code have therefore been removed. Branches that control symbol
reads retain the upstream structure to simplify comparison. The PVQ decoder
reads each codeword index and stops there: cwrsi(), which upstream uses to
turn the index into a pulse vector nothing here consumes, is gone.

The files are grouped as follows.

  opusdec.h                 parser API used by opusmode.c
  opus_dec.c                packet layout and frame dispatch
  entdec.c                  range-decoder operations routed through the model
  entcode.*, entenc.*       range coder
  celt*                     CELT parsing and tables
  silk*                     SILK parsing and tables
  arch.h, opus_*.h,
  os_support.h              shared definitions

Balrogg adds model hooks for the CELT Laplace and angle decoders. The CELT
parser also records the state needed by the model in the orec_* fields from
opusent.h.

For validation, compare archives with a full libopus build carrying the same
hooks. The outputs must be byte-identical.
